import Mathlib

/-! # CohomologyComparisonsPartII: target signatures

The roadmap is README.md; this file is not the roadmap. It states the roadmap's
headline theorems against the pinned Mathlib and Tau Ceti APIs when their carriers
are available. None of the following headline theorems is statable at these pins:

* Injectivity of extension evaluation when F⁰H = 0 (README §1.6) needs the category
  FilFMIC of filtered Frobenius connections, its exact-category Yoneda extensions
  and its coefficient connection complex; these carriers are absent.
* The unramified rigid syntomic fibre comparison (§2.3) needs rigid cohomology and
  filtered algebraic de Rham realizations, including their specialization map.
* Local log-PD realization, gluing and the rational syntomic fibre (§3.4) need
  log-scheme, log-crystalline coefficient and log-syntomic site carriers.
* The exact small-weight and bounded all-weight period comparisons, including
  syntomic-étale gluing (§§4.3–4.5), need the divided and undivided log-syntomic
  complexes and the étale Tate sheaves and nearby-cycle realizations on log schemes.
* The classical semistable fibre comparison and classical-to-h compatibility
  (§§5.2–5.3) need the Hyodo–Kato, classical syntomic and syntomic h-realizations
  of arithmetic pairs. The isocrystal carrier alone does not supply these objects.
* Geometric filtered Frobenius realization (§6.4) needs relative rigid and filtered
  de Rham cohomology and the category FilFMIC.
* The relative continuous-form comparison (§6.5) needs weak completions with their
  continuous differential complexes and the relative rigid realization.
* The strict open-curve residue sequence (§6.6) needs those relative realizations
  as objects of FilFMIC, including nonsplit finite étale boundary coefficients.
* Frobenius-point specialization of extension evaluation (§7.3) needs FilFMIC,
  its exact-category extensions and their connection-complex pullback.
* The horizontal-log/rigid syntomic comparison (§7.4) needs log-crystalline,
  filtered log de Rham and rigid syntomic realizations of the compactification pair.
* Absolute extension evaluation and its specialization equality (§7.5) need the
  geometric coefficient object, its extension group and the log/rigid syntomic
  cohomology targets.

These constructions belong to the README layers and their named suppliers.
-/

